        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.12,
            0.445,
            0.147
          ],
          "content": "and $\\frac { 6 } { 7 }$ will be represented as —"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.274,
            0.149,
            0.675,
            0.189
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_26_image_2.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.205,
            0.553,
            0.336
          ],
          "content": "In this case, the total number of shaded parts is 10, and each shaded part represents the fractional unit ${ \\frac { 1 } { 7 } } ,$ so, the 10 shaded parts together represent the fraction $\\frac { 1 0 } { 7 }$ as seen here."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.588,
            0.208,
            0.824,
            0.311
          ],
          "content": "While adding fractions with the same fractional unit, just add the number of fractional units from each fraction."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.273,
            0.339,
            0.675,
            0.416
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_26_image_5.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.239,
            0.426,
            0.487,
            0.542
          ],
          "content": "Therefore, $\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4}{7} + \\frac{6}{7} &= \\frac{10}{7} \\\\&= 1 \\pm \\frac{3}{7} \\\\&= 1\\frac{3}{7}\\end{aligned}$"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.241,
            0.553,
            0.644,
            0.629
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
